{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00659",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.45,
      "end_seconds": 14.02,
      "duration_seconds": 13.57,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I've been keeping a note of this, so I can be precise. My heart pounds at night, and has done for about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.15,
      "end_seconds": 21.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Thank you, that's really useful. Tell me what it feels like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.02,
      "end_seconds": 36.54,
      "duration_seconds": 12.52,
      "text": "A thumping, in the chest and sometimes in my throat, quite fast. It wakes me up, usually between two and four."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.91,
      "end_seconds": 42.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "How long does an episode last?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.52,
      "end_seconds": 51.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Anywhere from a couple of minutes to, last Tuesday, I'd say twenty minutes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 54.46,
      "end_seconds": 61.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "[from the corridor] It was nearer half an hour, last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.29,
      "end_seconds": 69.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "Oh, someone's talking out there. Ignore that. It lasted a good while, anyway."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.42,
      "end_seconds": 79.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "I'll go by what you tell me. Does anything come with it, dizziness, sweating?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.24,
      "end_seconds": 91.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.35,
      "text": "Dizzy spells, yes. Occasionally I feel light-headed when I stand up in the morning. I can't say when that began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.87,
      "end_seconds": 96.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Roughly, before the thumping, or after?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.56,
      "end_seconds": 103.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "I honestly don't know. I only noticed it recently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.64,
      "end_seconds": 111.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Fair enough. And do you sweat at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.02,
      "end_seconds": 119.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Sometimes, after the thumping. My pyjamas get damp."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.54,
      "end_seconds": 124.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Any chest pain with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.43,
      "end_seconds": 129.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "No pain, none whatsoever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.81,
      "end_seconds": 136.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Have you fainted, or come close to it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.72,
      "end_seconds": 139.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "No, never fainted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.67,
      "end_seconds": 148.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "What about caffeine and alcohol? Tell me what you have in a typical day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.42,
      "end_seconds": 161.45,
      "duration_seconds": 12.03,
      "text": "About four cups of strong tea, usually the last at around eight in the evening. And I drink wine at the weekend, a glass or two."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.07,
      "end_seconds": 165.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Any allergies to anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.81,
      "end_seconds": 169.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.66,
      "end_seconds": 173.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Let me check your numbers. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.12,
      "end_seconds": 177.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Please. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.86,
      "end_seconds": 210.24,
      "duration_seconds": 13.38,
      "text": "Pulse 74 and regular, blood pressure 124 over 78, temperature 36.6, oxygen 99 percent, breathing 14 a minute, and you weigh 66 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.76,
      "end_seconds": 214.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "All normal? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.04,
      "end_seconds": 221.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "All normal. Any cough or breathlessness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.63,
      "end_seconds": 225.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "No, my breathing is fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.73,
      "end_seconds": 232.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Any ankle swelling or tiredness, anything with the heart?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.34,
      "end_seconds": 237.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "No swelling. Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.49,
      "end_seconds": 260.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Let me listen. Breathe normally."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.84,
      "end_seconds": 265.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Is it a murmur? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.54,
      "end_seconds": 272.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "Your heart sounds are normal, no murmurs, and your pulse is regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.51,
      "end_seconds": 281.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "That's a relief. So what's causing the thumping? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.43,
      "end_seconds": 293.87,
      "duration_seconds": 11.44,
      "text": "Weighing it all up, the most likely cause is the caffeine, especially the tea late into the evening. I'd say caffeine-related palpitations."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.58,
      "end_seconds": 304.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "I have been drinking more since I took on the extra project. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.07,
      "end_seconds": 317.59,
      "duration_seconds": 11.52,
      "text": "That would do it. Cut the tea down to two cups, none after noon, and see what happens over the next fortnight."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.35,
      "end_seconds": 322.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Two cups. That will be a trial. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.5,
      "end_seconds": 336.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.29,
      "text": "And alcohol late in the evening can trigger it too, so keep the wine to earlier in the day. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.73,
      "end_seconds": 344.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "I'll bear it in mind. And if it doesn't stop? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.87,
      "end_seconds": 358.56,
      "duration_seconds": 12.69,
      "text": "Keep your diary going. If it gets worse, lasts more than half an hour, or you feel faint or get chest pain, come in straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.34,
      "end_seconds": 364.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Understood. Thank you for being so reassuring. ~"
    }
  ]
}
